.SS "void SystemEx\&.IByteSerializable< TSelf >\&.ToBytes (ref byte[] destination, long offset, \fBEndian\fP endian)"

.PP
Writes the binary representation of the current instance into an existing \fIdestination\fP  buffer at the specified \fIoffset\fP \&. The caller is responsible for ensuring that the buffer is large enough to hold the encoded data starting at the given offset\&. Bytes before the offset remain untouched and can contain arbitrary user data\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIdestination\fP The target buffer into which the encoded value will be written\&. 
.br
\fIoffset\fP The position within \fIdestination\fP  where the encoded data will be written\&. For example, if \fRoffset = 100\fP, bytes \fR0\fP through \fR99\fP remain unchanged, and the encoded value begins at index \fR100\fP\&. 
.br
\fIendian\fP The byte order used to encode the value\&. 
.RE
.PP

.PP
